&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title: Head of Data Management - Managing Director (NY)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Entity: KBRA Holdings, LLC&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employment Type: Full-time&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: New York, New York, United States&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Summary/Overview&lt;/u&gt;: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KBRA is seeking a senior leader to head our Data Management organization. Based in New York and reporting to the Chief Technology Officer, this individual will be responsible for defining and executing KBRA&#39;s enterprise data management strategy, leading Data Operations, advancing data governance and quality, and helping unlock the commercial value of KBRA&#39;s data assets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will work across analytical, business, product, and technology teams to establish how KBRA&#39;s data is organized, governed, curated, maintained, and made available for internal and external use. This is a highly visible leadership position requiring both strategic thinking and a willingness to engage directly in the details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;About the Job:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Head of Data Management will establish the operating model, standards, and capabilities necessary to manage KBRA&#39;s data as a strategic enterprise asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will lead the Data Operations organization and oversee disciplines including data stewardship, master and reference data management, taxonomy and ontology development, data quality, and data-provider management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working closely with Engineering and Product, you will help establish scalable data models, standards, processes, and technology capabilities that make KBRA&#39;s data easier to discover, integrate, govern, and use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will also partner with business leadership to identify opportunities to package and commercialize KBRA&#39;s proprietary data assets and to ensure those assets are supported by appropriate governance, quality, and operational processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute KBRA&#39;s enterprise data management strategy and operating model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop the Data Operations organization, including data stewardship, master/reference data management, data quality, taxonomy, and related disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage day-to-day operational delivery, service levels, controls, escalation and capacity planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish standards for the organization, classification, definition, ownership, and lifecycle management of KBRA data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continue to mature KBRA’s data governance and data quality programs by establishing measurable standards for accuracy, completeness, consistency, timeliness, and exception management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain an enterprise data-domain model, including data owners, stewards, authoritative sources, definitions, quality and lifecycle. Lead the development of taxonomies, ontologies, common definitions, and canonical data concepts across KBRA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering and Product on data architecture, data catalog/glossary development, metadata management, lineage, integration standards, and platforms supporting enterprise data management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure ratings-related data management processes, controls, lineage, and documentation meet applicable regulatory and audit expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a senior point of contact for regulators, auditors, and other stakeholders on matters related to ratings data management and operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with business leaders to identify, evaluate, and develop opportunities to commercialize KBRA&#39;s proprietary data assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, evaluate, and onboard third-party data providers that improve the quality, coverage, efficiency, or automation of KBRA&#39;s data processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and implement technology that automates and augments data ingestion, curation, matching, enrichment, stewardship, and quality management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish KPIs and operating metrics for data quality, operational performance, stewardship, and data-management effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure KBRA&#39;s data assets are discoverable, well-defined, governed, traceable, and of sufficient quality to support artificial intelligence, machine learning, semantic search, advanced analytics, and other emerging data-driven capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, develop, and retain a high-performing data management organization capable of scaling with KBRA&#39;s growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate as a member of the Technology Leadership Team and contribute to KBRA&#39;s broader technology, product, and data strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and oversee change governance for critical data definitions, taxonomies, reference data, identifiers, and business rules, including impact assessment, review, approval, documentation, and communication of changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead data-governance forums and cross-functional data decisions/escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;About You:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are an entrepreneurial and pragmatic leader who views data as both an operational capability and a strategic business asset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can establish a long-term vision while also working through complex implementation details. You are comfortable operating across business, analytical, product, engineering, and regulatory stakeholders and can translate between those audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are an effective communicator who can clearly articulate a data strategy, build organizational alignment around it, and lead teams through significant change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will Be Successful in This Role If You Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or master&#39;s degree or equivalent relevant experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of experience in data management, data strategy, data operations, data governance, or related disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant leadership experience building and managing data teams and capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within financial services, capital markets, ratings, financial data, or another data-intensive industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating within a regulated environment and working with risk, compliance, audit, or regulatory stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience establishing enterprise data governance, stewardship, and data quality programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with master data management, reference data, metadata management, taxonomy/ontology management, or data quality platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing data operating models, standards, policies, and ownership frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of modern data platforms, integration patterns, data lineage, and data lifecycle management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience evaluating and managing third-party data providers and data licensing relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience identifying or developing opportunities to commercialize data products or proprietary datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience building or materially transforming an enterprise data-management capability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build strong relationships with executives, analytical teams, product teams, engineers, customers, and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate enterprise objectives into a clear, executable data strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to tailor communication to senior executives, analytical professionals, regulators, and technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience preparing enterprise data for artificial intelligence, machine learning, semantic search, or other advanced analytical use cases is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Salary Range:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The anticipated annual base salary range for this full-time position is $225,000 to $300,000. Offer amounts are determined by factors such as experience, skills, geography, and other job-related factors.&lt;/p&gt;
